  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 123 PM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nTonight through Labor Day...High pressure aloft and at the surface \nwill remain in place across the region through the forecast period. \nThus, expect a continuation of humid conditions and hot \ntemperatures.  Highs each afternoon will warm into the middle and \nupper 90s. This, as dew points mix each day in the low and middle \n70s, will yield afternoon heat index values above the century mark. \nAs a result, a prolonged period of dangerous heat stress is \nexpected, with a \"Heat Advisory\" at a minimum needed for portions \nof, if not all of, the forecast area each day.\n\nOther than an isolated shower or storm being observed in the south \nand in the vicinity of the Highway 84 corridor today through \nWednesday, the CWA overall will remain dry.  As better moisture \nworks north into the forecast area Thursday into Labor Day weekend, \nbetter rain chances will likewise spread northward into the CWA. \nThis could bring some temporary relief from both the heat and dry \nconditions across the region, especially Friday through Labor Day. \n/19/",
